Myth: The silence in the cavern of the Mirror of Abundance had grown heavy, a shroud of hesitation born from the mist. Yet, the Sun-Giver remembered the rhythm of the dance. He understood that when the Earth-Tender’s hand remained closed, it was not an act of finality, but a tremor of fear in the face of the swirling fog. To leave the pool frozen was to accept the decay of their shared garden.

Gathering his resolve, the Sun-Giver stepped to the edge of the reflecting pool. He knew the risks: the water might swallow his gift, or the mist might distort the tally, creating shadows where there should be light. But he realized that trust is not a static reward for past actions; it is an active, recurring choice to bridge the void. With a steady heart, he cast his entire harvest into the depths, trusting that his offering would serve as a beacon, cutting through the haze of the previous silence. He chose to be the architect of a new beginning, planting a seed of faith in the sediment. He knew that for the garden to bloom again, someone had to be the first to break the stillness, proving that generosity is the only cure for doubt.

